The first whole-pattern checkpoint confirms two coherent reflection families: tetragonal scheelite CaWO₄ and monoclinic WO₃. Every prominent peak is already indexed, but the unconstrained profile fit traded instrumental and specimen broadening into nonphysical negative profile coefficients, so I’m rebuilding the checkpoint with fixed overall scale and physical parameter bounds before assessing residuals or fractions.

The bounded comparison is informative but exposed a calibration trap: refining zero and specimen height before the cells drove both to their prior limits and GSAS-II froze them, degrading later cell fits. The physically better neutron WO₃ parent remains under test, but I’m correcting the sequence by fitting cells with one calibration term at a time and explicitly unfreezing bounded variables after the metric settles.

